WEBVTT

0
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:09.560
Optical circuit switching is fundamentally reshaping today's AI data centers,

1
00:00:09.899 --> 00:00:15.090
but it is also the key to unlocking two massive frontiers in computing,

2
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:16.680
quantum networks

3
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.120
and resource disaggregation.

4
00:00:19.579 --> 00:00:21.500
Let us start with quantum networking.

5
00:00:22.149 --> 00:00:24.649
The fundamental bottleneck in this field

6
00:00:24.829 --> 00:00:26.649
is the extreme fragility

7
00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:28.149
of quantum information.

8
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.450
In traditional packet switched networks,

9
00:00:31.809 --> 00:00:34.119
signals undergo multiple optical,

10
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:34.930
electrical,

11
00:00:35.049 --> 00:00:36.590
optical conversions.

12
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.439
While this is fine for classical bits,

13
00:00:39.689 --> 00:00:41.709
it is fatal for quantum bits

14
00:00:41.849 --> 00:00:43.110
or qubits.

15
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.630
According to the no cloning theorem,

16
00:00:45.889 --> 00:00:50.409
quantum states cannot be copied or measured without being destroyed.

17
00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:56.020
An electrical switch must essentially read a packet in order to route it.

18
00:00:56.319 --> 00:00:59.459
This measurement causes immediate decoherence

19
00:00:59.599 --> 00:01:01.720
and collapses the quantum state.

20
00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:02.369
Because

21
00:01:02.759 --> 00:01:03.360
of this,

22
00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:08.019
standard buffered switches are physically incapable of supporting

23
00:01:08.199 --> 00:01:10.099
a future quantum internet.

24
00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.169
Optical circuit switching solves this

25
00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.410
by providing a transparent,

26
00:01:15.639 --> 00:01:17.540
all optical switching path.

27
00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:20.680
Because an OCS device redirects light

28
00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.069
without converting photons into electrical signals,

29
00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:28.199
the quantum states remain entirely within the optical domain.

30
00:01:29.069 --> 00:01:32.370
The switch functions more like a clear glass window.

31
00:01:33.769 --> 00:01:38.150
This preserves the high fidelity required for quantum teleportation

32
00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.370
and distributed quantum computing.

33
00:01:41.419 --> 00:01:43.139
Beyond the quantum realm,

34
00:01:43.459 --> 00:01:47.440
OCS is also transforming classical architecture

35
00:01:47.669 --> 00:01:49.699
through resource disaggregation.

36
00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:51.919
Resource disaggregation

37
00:01:52.019 --> 00:01:56.129
connects servers with pooled resources such as accelerators,

38
00:01:56.459 --> 00:01:57.080
memory,

39
00:01:57.339 --> 00:01:58.239
and storage.

40
00:01:59.019 --> 00:01:59.510
Currently,

41
00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:02.930
the effective reach of high-speed copper links

42
00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.459
continues to shrink at higher signaling rates.

43
00:02:06.209 --> 00:02:10.399
Extending this reach with fiber optics and electrical conversion

44
00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:12.679
adds unacceptable latency

45
00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:14.139
and power consumption.

46
00:02:14.899 --> 00:02:19.559
OCS technology offers compelling advantages for this use case,

47
00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:22.619
because it is inherently rate agnostic,

48
00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:27.520
it allows bandwidth to scale efficiently without reducing port count.

49
00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:28.889
Additionally,

50
00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:34.899
OCS avoids OEO conversion delays and eliminates queuing related latency.

51
00:02:36.199 --> 00:02:39.210
This enables the ultra low latency required

52
00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.190
for resource desegregation architectures.

53
00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:45.449
Whether preserving delicate cubits

54
00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:47.350
or accelerating memory,

55
00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:50.509
pure light is the ultimate transport layer.